fix = "Decision 2667: a page of the web router is proven at the controller through Phoenix.ConnTest bypass_through and the controller call; attempt 2 rewrites the two cases that way."

[gotcha.3243]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 3: both receipt-key cases pass; the first Prepare answers 503 owner.unavailable because the authority fixture of tests/native_send_preview_evm.rs (line 448, included by the task test) serves /v1/agent/registry, /v1/agent/subject-context and /v1/agent/identity and panics on any other route, while the Human runtime of the Prepare path reads /v1/agent/balance-context (src/human_runtime.rs line 1833); the peer drop then panics at line 107."
symptom = "The Prepare path reads the balance context after the subject context; tests/human_approval_budget_actor.rs line 419 and tests/repair_22_31_562.rs line 426 serve that route with the balance document, the preview fixture never did."
fix = "The scope now carries tests/native_send_preview_evm.rs; attempt 4 serves /v1/agent/balance-context with the balance document of those two tests and every further route the Prepare path reads (src/human_runtime.rs lines 1743 to 2095), and the peer drop reports instead of panicking."

[gotcha.3244]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 11: the batched Send verifies through the SDK (module 12 operation 2, pinned authority, coverage, inclusion) and the grant and draw receipts verify through the peer self-check; the daemon then refuses the cumulative-use evidence of the draw with Receipt(Receipt(VerificationFailure SequencerSignature)) at tests/support/funded_scenario.rs line 892."
symptom = "EvidenceAuthority verify_signed_receipt_inclusion (src/protocol_evidence.rs lines 441 to 458) verifies the receipt signature with verify_sequencer_signature under the batch authorization public key alone; a bare 32-byte key becomes ReceiptKeys::HistoricalKernel (layerx-proof receipt.rs line 42), and select_receipt_key refuses every module id above KERNEL_MODULE_COUNT 11 under that variant (lines 821 to 824). Node receipts carry module 12 and above (decision 2648), so the cumulative-use path authenticates no node receipt; verify_current_receipt in the same file (lines 640 to 660) already selects the governed receipt keys through SequencerAuthorization height ranges."
fix = "Decision 2666 and task 22.31.568 repair the daemon; 22.33.1569 requalifies on its attempt-11 tree once 22.31.568 is on main."

[gotcha.3245]
title = "22.33.1510 attempt 7: real_agent_holds_drive_live_inbox_counts_notifications_and_honest_lifecycle fails with Io PermissionDenied store root is not a canonical owned private directory (tests/approvals.rs line 28) and digest_bound_decisions_converge_and_export_the_agent_outcome with ApprovalBoundaryError Refused from the first approval_get (tests/decide.rs lines 29 and 270); the owner fixture tests/support/approval_owner.rs line 585 builds its root from std::env::temp_dir() without canonicalising it."
symptom = "store/protected.rs validate (lines 88 to 96) refuses a root whose canonical path differs from the path given, among four other conditions; the one existing test of this crate that opens an agent store, tests/production_unhooked.rs line 62, canonicalises temp_dir first. The decide case most likely fails downstream of the same refusal inside the owner thread (server/agent_runtime.rs line 4389 maps AgentBoundaryError::Refused); attempt 8 shows whether it does."
fix = "Attempt 8 builds the fixture root from fs::canonicalize(std::env::temp_dir()) as production_unhooked.rs does and prints the path, canonical path, uid and mode on any remaining refusal."

[gotcha.3246]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 9: build and 29 dependent-crate checks pass; TestRepair478_FundWithinProductionAllowance stops Fund with LXP_ERR_GAS_EXHAUSTED at 999968 of the 1000000 CPU fuel the call budget carries (rpc/repair_478_test.go line 305), as attempt 8 stopped at 999988; the Rust fuel table was not reached. The attempt removed the full-state reward validation on Fund, but the Fund path (rewards.rs fund at line 2266) still decodes the whole joint section into its view before the ledger head is updated and re-encodes through commit."
symptom = "The record shows only the exhaustion point, never the cost; two attempts have reduced Fund without a measurement. The decode of the dictionary, epoch rows and refund record that Fund carries byte-for-byte is the remaining cost no measurement has isolated."
fix = "Attempt 10 measures Fund under a test-only CPU budget of 4000000 and records the real cost before reducing; the reduction drops every decode of a carried region from the Fund path."

[gotcha.3247]
title = "22.31.567 attempt 1: the build fails at tests/repair_22_31_563.rs line 710, which calls with_node_commit_authority with the authority and a coverage argument, after the task narrowed the method to the authority alone (src/rpc_commit.rs line 67); the file is outside the task scope so the agent left it."
symptom = "The task listed the three callers it knew (tests/repair_22_31_494.rs, tests/support/audit_22_30_99.rs, src/wallet.rs) but not the test of the task it requires, which landed with the two-argument form the task retires."
fix = "The scope now carries tests/repair_22_31_563.rs; attempt 2 moves that call to the one-argument form with the coverage fetched per wait, and a signature change lists every caller a search of the main tree finds."

[gotcha.3248]
title = "22.31.566 attempt 1: the native result adapter maps the Bounds engine fault to -740 and every other ExecutionError Fault to -741, four of five cases pass, and trapping_guest_initializer_answers_guest_fault fails at tests/repair_22_31_566.rs line 133 with unwrap_err called on an Ok V2AuthorizedExecutionRecord: a guest whose start function traps under a replay profile comes back as a retained record, not as an executor error."
symptom = "execute_authorized_v2_with_budget (execute.rs lines 4458 to 4497) turns a start-function trap that left a trap record into a record through finish_v2_start (a Failure with the RuntimeFault class), and a trap inside the entry call is retained the same way (lines 4572 to 4586); the budgeted v2 path answers ExecutionError Fault only for engine conditions: a replay profile whose trace policy diverges from the executor policy (line 4444), a start failure without a trap record (4466), a missing start replay identity (4469), an execution observer fault without a trap record (4512 to 4518), a trace identity and policy divergence (4537) and a refused replay capture (4867). The task text and decision 2655 called -741 the guest fault; no guest trap reaches it."
fix = "-741 is the executor engine fault (decision 2668); the test proves it through a diverging trace policy and asserts the retained record for the trapping guest."

[gotcha.3249]
title = "22.31.566 attempt 1: the change to programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/ffi_call.rs is 8149 diff lines (4399 insertions, 4030 deletions) for a 95-line functional change: the attempt wrapped the whole binding in a nested module behind the host-ffi feature and re-indented about 4500 lines so that the test could include the file by path without the feature; the whitespace-insensitive diff is 156 insertions and 61 deletions."
symptom = "The declared gate does not enable host-ffi, so the adapter had to live outside the gated code; placing it at the top of the gated file forced the wrap, and the wrap destroys the line history of the binding."
fix = "The adapter moves to its own unconditional module file and ffi_call.rs changes only at the execute call site (decision 2668)."

[gotcha.3250]
title = "22.99.77 attempt 18 (after 22.31.564 landed): the executor proof of tests/support/native_replay.rs now answers ExecutionError Fault EngineFault deterministic execution observer refused: SupplementRejected for all twelve native CALLs at height 1000 (previously the CPU budget stop of gotcha 3223), the fuel table lists eight operations over the 1000000 cap (OPEN_EPOCH at 896 and 1024 state bytes, three RevealScore cases at 1104, ScheduleEvaluator, RotateEvaluatorKey and RevokeEvaluator at 1107), five view-binding cases fail on expectations the attempt rewrote (view_binding.rs lines 332, 676 and 1046), and reward_native_reopen stops at repair_22_33_261.rs line 1529 with an empty commit-process message."
symptom = "Every refusal in execution_supplement, measure_supplement_host, supplement_snapshot_bytes, uncollected_supplement and retain_boundary_capture (programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/host/mod.rs lines 301 to 316, 502 to 512, 551 to 600, 616 to 632 and 666 to 780) maps to the same SupplementRejected value and execute.rs lines 1471 and 1498 print only that value, so the fault cannot name its site; the 564 proof covers a guest without shared state, and before 564 the first supplement stopped at the CPU charge so the later sites never ran for a real guest. The rewritten a02 case asserts a lower-rank binding equal to the published one although the binding carries the evidence rank (the main-tree assertion at line 664 compared with the rank substituted); the uncreated-market case expects NotYetProduced where production answers ContentUnavailable; the a04 fixture is refused with application error 14 before the rows are read."
fix = "Task 22.31.569 makes the observer refusal name its site and admits a profiled CALL of a guest with a large shared state (decision 2669); 22.99.77 continues after it with the eight fuel residuals and the test expectations reconciled to production."

[gotcha.3251]
title = "22.36.5 attempt 1: the four documents are moved and eight of nine cases pass; test_no_tracked_references_to_old_document_paths fails because three tracked files outside the listed scope still name an old path: services/platform/perps-data/internal/records/records.go line 119 (a comment pointing at apps/perps/data_api.md), tools/qualification/audit_repairs/test_repair_22_33_1565.py lines 50, 80 and 110 (a live test that reads services/agent/COMPATIBILITY.md) and tools/qualification/audit_repairs/repair_22_33_1565.kvx line 16 (a repair record)."
symptom = "The task listed the files its grep found at authoring time by directory and missed two of them; the candidate test excludes only spec/, GOTCHA.kvx and itself, although decision 2665 excludes repair records from a retirement grep."
fix = "The test excludes repair records by pattern and the two live files join the scope and are rewritten (decision 2670)."

[gotcha.3252]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 4: the authority fixture serves balance-context and the peer drop reports the bootstrap failure once; the preview and the wrong-identifier refusal pass and the first Prepare still answers 503 owner.unavailable; the chain peer prints the next refused call, px_getCommit at height 50, answered Method not found by the EVM node."
symptom = "The native send Prepare checks the direct node interface: human_node.rs verify_direct_node_readiness (line 105) calls ServedCheckpoint::acquire_at_committed_block (read/checkpoint.rs line 182), which reads eth_blockNumber, eth_getBlockByNumber, px_getCommit and px_getValidators at the head, decodes the signed header against the served validator set under chain id 125 and requires the block hash to equal the header block hash, the block stateRoot to equal app_hash and the block timestamp to equal the header time (lines 221 to 229); the EVM node serves no px_ method and the attempt-3 interception covers px_getReceiptKeys only."
fix = "Serve px_getCommit and px_getValidators from the chain peer with the recorded checkpoint at height 64 and answer the head block with the recorded header hash, app hash and time."

[gotcha.3253]
title = "22.31.568 attempt 1: the sequencer signature of a node receipt verifies under the governed keys and the two refusal cases pass; the governed case fails with CumulativeUseError::Activity after the signature verifies."
symptom = "authenticate_cumulative_use (protocol_evidence.rs lines 857 to 858) and the time-window path (lines 1228 to 1229) map every receipt module id through ModuleId::from_u16, which knows the kernel modules 1 to 11 only (layerx-types payload.rs line 54); a node receipt carries module 12 (decision 2648) and never names a kernel module, so the activity binding refuses before any identity is compared."
fix = "Bind a node receipt to its entry by the activity identity and the activity type of the signed envelope, not by the receipt module (decision 2671)."

[gotcha.3254]
title = "22.33.1510 attempt 8: the fixture root is canonical with mode 0700 and the store no longer refuses; the snapshot case passes; the approvals case fails with Agent(Refused) and the decision case with Refused after the lost-reply reopen; the daemon log before each refusal shows only the recovery lines (writes admitted, protocol_consumed Some(0))."
symptom = "Two causes stack: the daemon maps every approval lookup and decision error to HumanOperationError::Refused without the originating error (human_runtime.rs lines 7523, 7524, 7534, 7537 and 7543), so no diagnostic names the refusal; and after a restart ApprovalRegistry::replay_tenant (policy/approval.rs line 203) restores only the PreparedActivity holds and the program terminals while the released terminal records that replay_released (line 242) decodes are not restored, so a decided approval is unknown to approval_get and to a replayed decision once the daemon reopens."
fix = "22.31.570 restores released terminal approvals on replay and carries the originating error in every Refused mapping; 22.33.1510 re-runs after it."

[gotcha.3255]
title = "22.35.9 attempt 2: the compile and all 18 tests pass, the bypass_through rendering of the chain page included; the task graph check refuses the symbol BlocksCount as not defined in the graph."
symptom = "The symbol list of the task names BlocksCount, which is an alias of Explorer.Chain.Cache.Counters.BlocksCount in the two controllers and not a definition in the tree; the graph resolves defined symbols only, and total_blocks, block_height and block_count resolve."
fix = "Drop the alias from the symbol list and requalify the attempt-2 tree unchanged."

[gotcha.3256]
title = "22.36.2 attempt 2: six of the seven cases pass (the retired paths are rewritten in the ten readers and in .gitignore, the human API page is regenerated, the repair records are excluded by pattern); test_documentation_tree_and_all_thirteen_samples_moved fails because services/platform/examples/samples/verify-receipt-rust/Cargo.lock is missing from the candidate although the attempt moved it with git mv and saw it tracked before the build; the recorded tree carries the old path deleted and no lock at the new path."
symptom = "The qualification environment builds the candidate from the touched paths and, under a touched directory, kept only the lock files the start tree tracked there, classing every other lock file as generated output; a lock file moved into the directory by the task was therefore dropped from the recorded commit. The rule was corrected at 02:28Z on 2026-11-06 to keep every lock file the index tracks under a touched directory as well; the correction reaches attempts started after that time, this attempt started at 02:12Z."
fix = "Restore the lock at the moved path from the content the old path had at the start revision, stage it, and re-run the gates (decision 2673)."

[gotcha.3257]
title = "22.36.1 attempt 1: the second verify passes all 92 cases after the first run repaired the parent-relative links in the six translated READMEs under docs; the attempt is then refused as out of scope for 255 files under the moved project directory under tools/ whose names carry a non-ASCII arrow (the provider bridge recordings), and the recorded tree lacks the two lock files the move carried (the pnpm lock at the directory root and core/control-plane/package-lock.json) although both are tracked in the index."
symptom = "git prints a path with a non-ASCII character quoted and octal-escaped (core.quotePath), and the qualification environment compared that quoted string against the touched directories, so none of the 255 names matched the directory they lie under; the lock files fell to the rule of gotcha 3256. Both rules are corrected: lock files since 02:28Z and path quoting since 02:37Z on 2026-11-06; this attempt started at 00:28Z."
fix = "Restore the two lock files from the start revision, stage them, and re-run the gates; the work itself does not change (decision 2674)."

[gotcha.3258]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 10: the two measuring Fund calls the attempt-9 ruling asked for (CPU allowance 4000000) return LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL at 0 fuel before the guest runs; the production Fund on the candidate guest consumes 896330 CPU fuel, under the 1000000 cap for the first time, and returns LXP_ERR_PROGRAM_REFUSED with terminal kind 2; the Rust tests were not reached."
symptom = "The ruling named a budget the runtime cannot admit: every activity runs under the smaller of the executor budget and the protocol budget (effective_activity_maximum, programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/execute.rs line 3427), DeclaredBudget::new refuses a declaration above the protocol budget (budget.rs line 202) and the native binding maps that refusal to NON_CANONICAL before execution (ffi_call.rs lines 2603 to 2611). The refusal of the production Fund is a guest application result: the response bytes carry the u16 error code (ai-market lib.rs failure at line 263 through codec ApplicationResult::failure), and the Go test logs neither status nor response for a Fund result, so the cause stays unnamed."
fix = "Drop the over-cap measuring calls (decision 2675), log the status and response of every Fund result, decode the application error, and prove the Fund through the runtime executor in the Rust fuel table first (decision 2647) before repairing the path."

[gotcha.3259]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 12 (requalify after 22.31.568): the build of the funded qualification tests stops with E0061 at tests/support/funded_peer.rs line 528 and pay2e_test.rs line 69: with_node_commit_authority takes one argument but the attempt-11 tree passes the authority and a NodeCommitCoverage; the verify did not run."
symptom = "22.31.567 (on main since fe3fe074b7) changed the SDK interface: with_node_commit_authority pins the Comet trust only (layerx-sdk src/rpc_commit.rs line 67) and every committed wait acquires its own sequence-batch coverage by reading px_getSequenceBatch with the height as a decimal string (rpc_verification.rs line 349), decoding height, tx (the 241-byte batch envelope) and proof (total, index, leafHash, aunts) and taking the activity ids in batch order from the transactions list of the served block (from_sequence_batch, rpc_commit.rs); the debug-only with_node_commit_coverage_override stays for the SDK crate tests. The funded peer predates that interface and still hands the coverage to the client."
fix = "Serve px_getSequenceBatch and the block transactions list from the funded peer and pin the authority alone (decision 2676); the task now requires 22.31.567."

[gotcha.3260]
title = "22.33.1510 attempt 9 (continue after 22.31.570): build exit 0, dependent-crate check exit 0, verify exit 101; 1 of 3 cases passes. approvals.rs line 196 fails in Inbox::consume(Granted) with Agent(Refused) and decide.rs line 424 fails because track_released answers Err(Refused) where the test expects Err(NotFound); the diagnostics print track_released(reference) = Err(Refused) beside both calls after the approval itself was granted, recovered and replayed correctly."
symptom = "The Human service tracks a granted approval by its release reference: approvals/mod.rs line 523 and approvals/decide.rs line 322 call track_released(submission_ref) and server/agent_runtime.rs line 4336 writes TRACK with that reference. The daemon release reference is ApprovalSubmissionQueue::reference (approval/mod.rs, sha256 of the tenant, the approval id and the unsigned preparation), held in the queue and journaled under the approval-released-v1 outbox records; TRACK (human_runtime.rs track_evm line 12613 and track_with_settlement line 13212) resolves only entries of the submissions set keyed by the submitting principal and the submission id, which the SUBMIT paths fill (lines 8564, 12941, 22364) and the start restores (line 13839), and refuses every other reference. No path links a release reference to the submission the agent later sends with approval_release_ref (lines 8044, 8239, 8437, 8731 and 8850), so the consumer can never track a release. The NotFound the decide case expected is unreachable by construction: map_approval_error (agent_runtime.rs line 4387) maps Unavailable, Refused and Corrupt only."
fix = "22.31.571 makes TRACK resolve a release reference of the tenant of the peer from release (Queued) through the linked submission to the verified receipt (decision 2677); 22.33.1510 continues after it, asserting the tracked state instead of a refusal."

[gotcha.3261]
