[gotcha.3268]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 14 (requalify of the attempt-13 tree): the build passed and the funded proof reached the grant draw, which the SDK verified with pinned node authority; the first authenticate_cumulative_use call at tests/support/funded_scenario.rs line 892 then refused the same draw receipt with Receipt(Receipt(VerificationFailure SequencerSignature))."
symptom = "The peer serves the draw as a module 12 receipt (decision 2648), so verify_signed_receipt_inclusion in layerx-agentd protocol_evidence.rs (lines 451 to 483) verifies its signature against the governed receipt keys of the evidence authority, not against the batch-header authorization; the authority the proof builds in pay2_evidence_authority (funded_scenario.rs lines 331 to 372) comes from the boot gate, whose evidence_authority (boot.rs lines 123 to 140) returns the authority loaded at Gate::new with an empty receipt-key list (protocol_evidence.rs line 607), and the readiness gate only checks the node keys against the handshake policy without installing them (boot.rs lines 85 to 97). select_receipt_key in layerx-proof receipt.rs (lines 800 to 826) finds no key and answers SequencerSignature. The daemon runtime installs the node keys before verifying (human_runtime.rs lines 12333 to 12344, with_receipt_keys over receipt_keys of the chain); the proof never did."
fix = "Install the readiness receipt keys into the proof authority with with_receipt_keys, as the runtime does (decision 2682)."

[gotcha.3269]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 1: the retained-state delta accounting, the quantified refusals and the proof were implemented and the build passed; the dependent-crate check stopped with exit 101 on the layerx-agentd compat.rs include (gotcha 3263; the attempt started at 03:37Z, before 22.31.572 reached main at 03:49Z) and the verify never ran. The task record also states that the 128 host calls requested under a 128-boundary profile cannot fit: the proof keeps the assertion as written and it would fail."
symptom = "The translator emits one observe point per source instruction (vendored wasmi func_builder/translator.rs line 102, begin_operator) and with interval 1 every observed step is a retained snapshot bounded by maximum_boundaries (execution_trace.rs lines 418 to 422); the replay identity binds interval 1 and at most 4096 commitments (execute.rs lines 1216 and 5736). A host call in the proof guest is seven source instructions, so 128 calls need about 900 boundaries, and a real market operation near 1000000 fuel runs far more than 4096 source instructions. A call payload carries a replay profile only when it starts with the 34-zero-byte prefix (src/modules/programs/call.c lines 2902 to 2911; a plain payload decodes as an ordinary call and replay_profile answers None at ffi_call.rs line 1343), and a profiled call must publish a record (ffi_call.rs lines 2900 to 2903)."
fix = "The many-call proof runs under the kernel maximum 4096 with a host-call count whose leaves fit the witness bytes, and the market harness sends plain payloads for the twelve real operations (decision 2683); the attempt continues after the include repair that is on main."

[gotcha.3270]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 15: the build passes and the verify stops in the funded scenario with the panic PAY2 authenticated issue usage: Sequence raised by verify_cumulative_window; the loopback peer serves every batch as a singleton (header fields 5 and 6 both equal to the activity sequence, one leaf under the receipt root), so the consumer computes an activity count of zero and refuses the window."
symptom = "verify_cumulative_window (protocol_evidence.rs lines 794 to 799) takes activity_count = last_sequence minus first_sequence and requires it above zero, then requires leaf_count = activity_count + 1, leaf_index = expected leaf and global_sequence = first + leaf per entry, and chains batches by first = covered_until, batch_number + 1 and previous_state_root = the previous resulting root. The human runtime (line 13119), hash.rs receipt_execution_batch_id_maintenance (receipt sequence in [first, last), maintenance global_sequence = last) and the kernel maintenance envelope (src/protocol/lxp_maintenance.c line 218, global_sequence = header last_sequence) all model a protocol-3 batch as its activities at first to last minus one plus one maintenance leaf at last_sequence; a batch of one activity therefore spans two sequences and two leaves. The peer encoder (funded_peer.rs lines 905 to 957) writes fields 5 and 6 from the same sequence and builds the receipt root over one leaf (line 919)."
fix = "The peer serves the maintained shape of decision 2684: per activity n the batch covers sequences 2n minus 1 and 2n with batch number n, a receipt tree of the canonical receipt and a self-verified occupancy maintenance leaf."

[gotcha.3271]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 6: build, dependent-crate check and the preview and wrong-identifier cases pass; native_send_first_prepare_and_reopened_prepare_match_owner_preview fails at tests/repair_22_31_560.rs line 457 with PolicyRefusal owner.refused (request 80, Terminal) on the first PREPARE after the preview. The test chain peer answered the 0x1004 identity reads and the 0x101a ledger reads (getAsset, accountId, accountOwner, balanceOf, nextSequence) twice each and no 0x101b budget read was requested, so the refusal falls between the ledger reads and read_native_effect_budget_sources."
symptom = "The native PREPARE path has several silent Refused returns in that span on the attempt-6 tree: committed_prepared_caps and the fee state root and observed sequence checks (human_runtime.rs lines 7145 to 7156, fn at 23132 with the app hash comparison at 23141), the with_native_preparation closure around verify_native_owner_send_purpose and inspect_native_send_capability (7158 to 7190), the native effect policy lookup by transport tenant (7199 to 7206), authenticated_native_policy_usage per rate window through the node history with export trust (7207 to 7213, fn at 14087) and the caps freshness against the fee (7214 to 7218); the daemon logs nothing on Refused and owner.refused is the mapping of every one of them (agent_rpc.rs line 644, agent_rpc_adapters.rs line 743, the routing module line 609), so the evidence cannot name the site."
fix = "Trace the refusing site with a temporary print that never enters the commit, name it in the task record and repair the fixture it reads; no production change."

[gotcha.3272]
title = "22.31.566 attempt 3: the C codec test and the six Rust proof cases pass; TestLXPRevertTable fails at precompiles/common/lxp_errors_test.go line 228 expecting LXP_UNKNOWN for value -740 and reading LXP_REPLAY_BOUND; the Python check never ran."
symptom = "Line 227 of that test lists 1, -9, -99, -740 and -999 as values without a name; the task assigns -740 to LXP_ERR_REPLAY_BOUND and -741 to LXP_ERR_ENGINE_FAULT (include/layerx/lxp_result.h lines 150 to 151, lxp_errors.go lines 158 to 159), so the old unknown sentinel became a named code and the consumer test still asserts the old sentinel; the test file is not in the task touches."
fix = "Amend the touches, move the unknown sentinel to -742 (unassigned everywhere) and keep the -1000 and -1004 empty-name assertions."

[gotcha.3273]
title = "22.33.260 attempt 4: seven of eight cases pass after the shared BAD_VERSION decoding fix; aggregation_storage_admission_refusal panics at tests/repair_22_33_260.rs line 1433 because the retry of the first ProcessAggregation envelope after the committed admission is Routed::Refused where the test expects Routed::Unchanged."
symptom = "The retry replays the payload built at line 1406 with expected cursor 0 while the committed admission moved the cursor to 1 (asserted at line 1431). process (aggregation.rs lines 1073 to 1095) reads the expected cursor from the payload, checks the sealed input digest, and refuses STALE_CURSOR whenever the expected cursor differs from the sealed cursor before it reaches the already-applied branch; that branch answers AlreadyApplied only when the expected cursor matches and the phase is Terminal or the cursor equals the roster count. The routing module turns the refusal into Routed::Refused (line 899). The documented contract (lines 1282 to 1283) says the same: STALE_CURSOR for any other expected cursor, read the current one with progress."
fix = "The test retries with the current cursor read from the recovered state (1, which equals the one-participant roster count, so the answer is AlreadyApplied) and asserts the stale replay separately as Refused with the state unchanged; no production change."

[gotcha.3274]
title = "22.31.571 attempt 2: the build stops with E0308 at tests/repair_22_31_571.rs line 1067: SigningPreparation::restore takes a Store reference and the test passes a reference to must(shared.lock()), so the generic must is inferred as Result of Store and the mutex guard does not coerce; no verify ran and the record shows one build gate only."
