fix = "Bind the guard to a local and pass a reference to it; the production change (203 lines in human_runtime.rs, 235 in policy/approval.rs, 14 in outbox/recover.rs) is untested until the gates run."

[gotcha.3275]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 2: build and dependent-crate check pass; the first verify fails program_replay actual_module_start_refuses_unobservable_start_state with an EngineFault (preauthorized execution commitment accounting diverged from canonical state at step 5), which the repair cycle fixed (4 passed in the second verify); the second verify then fails the terminal decoder persistence case of repair_22_31_259 at line 957 with DigestMismatch from the settlement attach function, and the repair_22_31_564, repair_22_31_569 and repair_22_31_573 binaries never ran because cargo stops at the first failing test binary."
symptom = "22.31.488 (commit 87f25cefc8, 2026-11-05) made the settlement attach function of src/terminal (the storage-environment module, lines 296 to 318) take the canonical usage receipt bytes followed by their 32-byte sha256 digest and added append_receipt_digest (line 80), which the native host (host_ffi.rs line 853) and the 488 proof (tests/repair_22_31_488.rs lines 71 to 72) use; the 259 proof still passes the bare canonical_usage_receipt bytes (lines 945 and 957), so the reader takes the trailing transfer root as the digest. Only the 573 verify runs the 259 suite, the storage-environment module is identical to main on the attempt-2 tree, and the break has been on main since 488 landed."
fix = "Task 22.31.574 frames the receipt in the 259 proof (decision 2685); 573 requires it and continues with its own binaries run first."

[gotcha.3276]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 12: build and dependent-crate check pass after the compatibility include repair; the verify stops before any test runs because the Go test binary of rpc does not compile: rpc/repair_478_test.go line 382 calls balance.FillBytes on the value host.ReadBalance returns, which is the SDK Int of sdk/types/int.go and has no FillBytes method; the Rust market suite never ran."
symptom = "The SDK Int wraps a big.Int and exposes it through BigInt() (int.go line 84) and the arithmetic and comparison methods; FillBytes belongs to big.Int. The proof transports the observed balance to the Rust fixture as 16 big-endian bytes and must take the big integer first; line 418 of the same proof already uses the Int method Int64 correctly."
fix = "balance.BigInt().FillBytes(make([]byte, 16)) at line 382; no production change."

[gotcha.3277]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 16: the maintained batch shape of decision 2684 is accepted (the Sequence refusal is gone) and the funded path now stops at funded_scenario.rs line 900, PAY2 authenticated issue usage: Activity, from authenticate_cumulative_use on the entry that layerx_mcp::tools::wallet::cumulative_evidence builds from the verified first draw."
symptom = "The entry carries the exact submitted activity of the wallet execution (layerx-sdk rpc_verification.rs lines 73 to 84), which for a ledger operation is the signed EIP-1559 transaction the SDK sends under decision 2521; the daemon consumer (layerx-agentd protocol_evidence.rs lines 857 to 872 and the time-window twin at lines 1235 to 1262) only knows signed LayerX activity envelopes: peek_signed_activity_type refuses the 0x02 envelope and the refusal maps to CumulativeUseError::Activity before any receipt comparison. The node names such an activity by its transaction hash (node/sequencer/accept.go line 88, etx.Hash()) and its actor by the recovered sender; task 22.31.568 proved the node-receipt key path with a LayerX envelope only, so no production consumer ever accepted a real node activity."
fix = "Task 22.31.575 teaches both consumers the EVM transaction activity (transaction hash as the activity id, recovered sender as the actor bound to a caller-supplied account), decision 2687; 22.33.1569 requires it and continues on the attempt-16 tree."

[gotcha.3278]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 7: the instrumented trace of gotcha 3271 found the first silent refusal (the absent native session scope, human_runtime.rs line 7191, Session ScopeDenied) and the fixture now sends the signed local grant; the next run reached authenticated_native_policy_usage and px_getHistory was unserved, the peer now serves the authenticated ten-second history window; the third run passes session admission, the complete committed inventory and the history proof and the genuine first Prepare still answers 403 owner.refused with no diagnostic line, so the task ended its repair budget without the site."
symptom = "rpc_prepare_native_send (human_runtime.rs lines 7010 to 7461 of the attempt tree) maps about thirty distinct conditions to HumanOperationError::Refused without naming any of them: empty rate proofs, the budget source read, the fee policy bound, the owner purpose verification, the capability inspection, the durable preparation decode and its identity checks; the RPC surface collapses every one to the same owner.refused rejection. Each attempt can locate one site only by re-instrumenting the daemon, and the temporary prints are removed before qualification, so the next attempt starts blind again."
fix = "Decision 2688: the native send Prepare path reports the refusing site in the daemon diagnostic log as production behaviour, with the same private-log print that budget_read_parts already uses; the attempt-7 tree stands and the next attempt reads the site from the verify log and repairs the fixture for it."

[gotcha.3279]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 3: build and the dependent-crate check pass, program_replay and repair_22_31_259 pass (the 574 frame holds), then the verify stops in repair_22_31_564 at line 146: replay_capture_still_refuses_byte_and_boundary_profile_limits expects the reason deterministic execution observer refused: SupplementRejected and the runtime answers the same reason with the suffix at retain_boundary_capture.source; the 573 and 569 binaries never ran."
symptom = "Task 22.31.569 (landed as 9c0e7abe03) named the execution observer supplement refusal site in host/mod.rs line 603 and its own proof asserts the sited text (repair_22_31_569.rs line 206), but its verify ran only its binary, so the older 564 proof that asserts the unsited text has been red on main since that landing; the 573 verify lists 564 and stops there (decision 2685)."
fix = "Decision 2689: a producer that adds a site to a refusal reason runs every proof asserting that reason and amends them to the sited text; 573 amends tests/repair_22_31_564.rs within the task and continues."

[gotcha.3280]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 13: the Go proof compiles after the BigInt fix and runs: the baseline Fund exhausts the CPU allowance at 999975 fuel as recorded, the candidate Fund completes guest execution at 896330 CPU fuel under the 1000000 cap and then ends LXP_ERR_PROGRAM_REFUSED (-736) in the occupancy settlement callback (stage 5) because the proof advances the host block from 1002 to 1003 (repair_478_test.go line 363) without the occupancy finalization of 1002 that the ledger requires; the Rust diagnostic example (examples/repair_478_fixture.rs line 17) panics on the kernel terminal wrapper, terminal-applied-legs/v1, instead of decoding it. The agent stopped and asked because the attempt-13 note limited Go proof edits to compiler fixes."
symptom = "The allowance goal of the task is reached in the candidate tree; both remaining failures are fixture setup the gate exposed, and the note scope was read as forbidding their repair."
fix = "Decision 2690: a fixture correction the gate exposes is within a continue note when it uses production paths and keeps every assertion; 478 continues with both corrections."

[gotcha.3281]
title = "22.31.571 attempt 3: the build and the dependent-crate check (15 crates) pass and the TRACK proof reaches PREPARE, which answers status 1 operation.refused with no diagnostic (tests/repair_22_31_571.rs line 1073); recovery admits writes. In its last cycle the agent found that the proof encoded the PREPARE and SUBMIT body-digest text lengths as 64-bit values where the daemon hashes 32-bit lengths (human_runtime.rs hash_text, line 20011), corrected both encoders, and could not re-run the verify because the repair budget was spent; the correction is in the tree unverified."
symptom = "The gated prepare path (human_runtime.rs prepare_gated, the body-digest check at line 15293 and 19 further Refused mappings behind it) answers every refusal as operation.refused, so a proof-frame digest mismatch is indistinguishable from an actor, authority, nonce or policy refusal; the proof encoder was written from the submit digest helper that uses 64-bit lengths (subscription_create_digest) instead of hash_text."
fix = "Continue at the same tree: run the gates first; if PREPARE still refuses, decision 2691 adds the sited diagnostic to the Human journey prepare path, as decision 2688 did for native send, and the site names the next repair."

[gotcha.3282]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 4: the build, the dependent-crate check (58 crates) and the four recorded suites pass, the 564 reason amendment is in, and two 573 cases fail: the eight-call case is refused by the legacy execution trace guard, execution trace peak retained bytes 333376350 exceed 67108864 (execute.rs line 893), after the observer admitted it; the 128-call case is refused SupplementRejected at retain_boundary_capture.source because every boundary witness carries the 4096-byte baseline storage value in both the host and the storage preimages, seven boundaries per read, so even 65 reads exceed the 1048576-byte witness bound. The agent stopped for direction because commit.rs is out of scope and no check may be disabled."
symptom = "The legacy ExecutionTrace materializes every full canonical state (17 pages each) beside the replay record and sums them in execute.rs and commit.rs, so a default-stack guest can never stay under its 64 MiB guard whatever the observer charges; and the proof baseline value is a fixture choice that scales the witness."
fix = "Decision 2692: under a replay profile the replay record is the commitment and the legacy trace is not materialized; the proof baseline storage value shrinks to 32 bytes so the 128 reads fit the witness bound."

[gotcha.3283]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 17: the account-bound evidence of 22.31.575 passes the cumulative-use checks; the funded MCP identity registration then fails BoundaryUnavailable at funded_scenario.rs line 138 after the loopback peer served eth_call to the address precompile, the identity sequence, eth_blockNumber, eth_getBlockByNumber 6 twice, px_getCommit 6 and px_getValidators 6; the agent added the missing peer responses in two cycles and ran out of budget."
symptom = "The qualification resolver (services/agent/qualification/pay2/sequence.rs, resolve from line 124) maps four distinct boundary reads to BoundaryUnavailable without naming which; the last of them, CommittedReads::open (layerx-agentd src/read/committed.rs line 719), authenticates the served checkpoint through the production verifier over the commit and the validator keys, so a served commit the keys did not sign is reported as an unavailable boundary."
fix = "Decision 2693: the resolver prints the failing read; the peer serves a checkpoint for the committed height that the production verifier authenticates."

[gotcha.3284]
title = "22.35.8 attempts 2 to 4: each run reached the result collection step and was ended by the qualification environment past its deadline grace; no result of those runs exists. The collection step added the changed explorer directories (thousands of files under apps/explorer/ui and apps/explorer/toolkit) to the candidate index one file at a time, rewriting the whole monorepo index per file, so every collection took 17 to 30 minutes."
symptom = "The per-file add was invisible on small tasks; the explorer restyle tasks change whole directories."
fix = "The collection step adds every file of a directory entry in one call and prints its timing; the collection step gets a grace of its own. Attempt 1 at 38bc60fa64 is the only tree and continues."

[gotcha.3285]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 8: the sited refusal helper prints native send prepare refused at budget source read; the first-Prepare case gets 403 owner.refused because budget/program_sources.rs lines 433 and 564 refuse caps.level() below STATE_PROVEN, and read/committed.rs CommittedCaps::level (lines 166 and 420) answers CHECKPOINT_FINALISED for every committed read."
symptom = "In layerx-types verify.rs the deprecated CheckpointFinalised rank orders below Unverified (the Ord keys CheckpointFinalised and SettlementAnchored to 0 and 1, the live ranks to wire rank plus 2), so a committed read never satisfies a STATE_PROVEN floor; the daemon-wide retirement of the label is 22.31.539, which waits on 560."
fix = "Decision 2694: the two level() sites answer COMMITTED now; 22.31.539 keeps the rest of its scope."

[gotcha.3286]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 18: the served checkpoint authenticates, the SDK Send verifies to Batched with pinned authority and coverage, the MCP grant issue executes and its executed receipt is served, then wait_batched (funded_scenario.rs line 598) fails InvalidRequest before any further peer request."
symptom = "Wallet::wait_for_submitted (layerx-sdk wallet.rs line 220) refuses a receipt without canonical activity (rpc_verification.rs submitted_activity line 80); the MCP wallet execute (layerx-mcp tools/wallet.rs lines 97 to 115) waits through Wallet::wait_for and never binds the signed bytes, unlike Wallet::send and Wallet::payment (wallet.rs lines 78 to 80 and 262 to 266); the MCP cumulative_evidence (line 312) refuses the same receipts."
fix = "Decision 2695 and task 22.31.576: the SDK exposes a wait that binds the signed bytes and the MCP execute uses it; 1569 continues after 576."

[gotcha.3287]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 14: the build and the dependent-crate check pass, every prior block and block 1002 finalize through the production host-module path, and the candidate Fund answers the canonical synthetic pre-runtime failure with code -3 (LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL), recorded CPU fuel 0 and no callback stage; the fixture binary panicked decoding that bare terminal as an applied-legs wrapper (examples/repair_478_fixture.rs line 17), the second repair selected the decoder by tag, and the budget ended before it ran under a gate."
symptom = "The -3 at pre-runtime with zero fuel is the native binding mapping of an executor error or a missing replay record of a profiled CALL (decision 2647, ffi_call.rs lines 2896 to 2902), not a fuel stop; the Go case reads only the terminal, so the cause is in the independent executor result the fixture now prints."
fix = "Attempt 15 runs the standing tree once, reads the executor result and repairs the cause it names."

[gotcha.3288]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 5: the build, the dependent-crate check (58 crates) and four recorded suites pass, the baseline value is 32 bytes and the proof searches for the largest admitted count; the 128-call case is refused SupplementRejected at retain_boundary_capture.source and the 65-call case is refused program replay record refused: Bounds, so no count above 64 fits the 1048576-byte witness."
symptom = "A portable boundary leaf carries the whole linear memory of the guest (portable_replay.rs line 128 reads it as one owned field up to MAX_STEP_STATE_BYTES; the proof asserts 17 pages, 1114112 bytes, in every leaf), so one leaf of a 17-page guest is larger than the kernel maximum of 1048576 witness bytes (programs.h line 677) and no profile the kernel accepts holds even one boundary of such a guest; the native CALL refusals of 22.99.77 under the 128-boundary 1 MiB profile are the same bound."
fix = "Decision 2696: a leaf carries the memory pages the boundary changed; 573 implements it and measures; 22.99.77 inherits it through 573."

[gotcha.3289]
title = "22.31.571 attempt 4: SUBMIT with the approval release reference now passes and the linked TRACK by reference equals the direct TRACK before the restart (byte 73 is 3, Submitted); after the Store is reopened and the runtime rebuilt the linked TRACK answers 5 (Unknown) at byte 73 and the proof stops at the assertion that the linked status survives restart (tests/repair_22_31_571.rs line 1199)."
symptom = "Production recovery restores a Submitted submission without a verified receipt as Unknown with the reason that the restart made the transport outcome indeterminate and lists it for receipt resolution (outbox/recover.rs restore_submissions, lines 233 to 243); the direct TRACK answers 5 after a restart as well, so the linked path mirrors the producer and the proof asserted a state recovery never keeps. The later assertion that the verified receipt survives restart (Executed, 6) is right because Executed restores unchanged in the same mapping."
fix = "The proof asserts the production recovery state after the first restart: byte 73 is 5 and the linked answer equals the direct TRACK taken after the same restart; decision 2697."

[gotcha.3290]
title = "22.31.573 attempt 6: the agent stopped at the reader condition of decision 2696 before changing the leaf encoding: the native market single-step adjudication opens one or two leaves by index against the trace root (execute.rs decode_market_step_evidence and open_market_boundary, lines 6258 to 6288 and 6020 to 6049), decodes the complete linear memory of the pre leaf (portable_replay.rs line 128) and replays that single boundary natively through the market step observer at line 5728, so a leaf that carries only the pages changed since the previous leaf leaves the adjudicator without the memory it replays; the build passed, no verify ran, the attempt-5 tree is preserved."
symptom = "Two consumers want two shapes of the same memory: the record witness needs small leaves (the whole record fits 1048576 bytes) and the single-step adjudicator needs the whole pre memory from one leaf. Decision 2696 served the first and broke the second. The kernel reader in src/modules/programs/call.c (lines 2968 to 3030) only hashes opaque leaves; the market program passes the evidence bytes through untouched (layerx-programs-market lib.rs lines 1298 and 1355), and the 259 and market proofs build their leaves at test time, so the encoding can change without recorded vectors."
fix = "Decision 2698: a leaf commits to its memory through a chunk root and carries the changed chunks; the adjudication evidence supplies the pre memory chunks that root authenticates. Task 22.31.577 implements it; 573 follows it and 22.99.77 inherits through 573."

[gotcha.3291]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 19: registration, the SDK Send, the SDK grant issue and draw and the MCP grant issue (batched wait) pass; the MCP grant draw is refused with WalletToolError::Arguments before submission (tests/support/funded_scenario.rs line 8 reports PAY2 MCP grant draw execution: Arguments)."
symptom = "policy_dimensions in services/agent/crates/layerx-mcp/src/tools/wallet.rs (line 256; the DrawGrant arm at lines 278 to 287) requires a Payment::Receive in the payment field of the disclosure, but bind_call for ConstructMethod::LedgerDraw (layerx-crypto disclosure/call.rs lines 968 to 981) sets only the counterparties, the Transfer amount and the idempotency key and never the payment field, since the draw calldata carries no payer and no asset; prepare_alias_call (wallet.rs lines 124 to 150) decodes the Receive with Payment::decode and discards it. The SDK draw path never consults policy_dimensions, so SDK draws pass."
fix = "Repair task 22.31.578 derives the DrawGrant policy dimensions from the decoded Receive cross-checked against the bound LedgerDraw (decision 2699); 22.33.1569 requalifies after it."

[gotcha.3292]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 9: after the denomination repair (reopen_daemon keeps the tenant-bound limit and attaches the protected denomination through attach_program_budget_denominations) the second verify run moves the refusal from the prepared cache lookup to native rate staging: services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs line 7374 answers owner.refused native rate staging and native_send_first_prepare_and_reopened_prepare_match_owner_preview fails (403 against 200 at tests/repair_22_31_560.rs line 622); the other 2 cases pass."
symptom = "StagedNativeRateUse::stage (layerx-agentd src/approval/native_program.rs lines 1333 to 1420) answers one CarrierError::Binding for every condition it checks: the disclosure binding, the canonical digest and the preparation id of the prepared bytes, the actor against the binding agent, an empty constraint chain or rate-obligation window set, an evidence count unequal to the window count, each window proof (actor, through_sequence equal to observed_head_sequence, observed_core_ms equal to the constraint observed_at_ms, window in the set, one observed batch id, no duplicate window) and the pending-use advance; the fixture evidence comes from operations.authenticated_native_policy_usage per window (human_runtime.rs near line 7224) and the test verifies history.time_window for a complete empty ten-second window (lines 876 to 890), so the refused equality is not visible from the log."
fix = "Attempt 10 adds a diagnostic inside stage naming the refused condition and repairs the fixture proof against the binding equalities; no production check is relaxed."

[gotcha.3293]
title = "22.33.1536 attempt 8: the gates passed at 34a1e6edcd856709cbac864b9843b542a03e018f but publication stopped on a three-way conflict in services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/human_node_budgets.rs: the attempt changed lines 79, 92, 161 and 204 and added a 49-line case after line 503 while main (dbd4e68ed9, the part-2 task) changed the signed_receipt lines 204 (paymentDenom and feeDenom) and 208 (signingKey from the public key)."
symptom = "The attempt branched from 61612c2b19a7 before the part-2 landing and both sides edited the same signed_receipt literal; the merge cannot choose."
fix = "Attempt 9 replays the attempt-8 changes onto the main version keeping the main-side paymentDenom and signingKey lines, then reruns the gates."

[gotcha.3294]
title = "22.33.1135 attempt 1: the gates passed at 584642067465bfa30d22a870958c22b659179f38 but the qualified tree changed tests/codec/generate_nfc_tables.py, two codec tests, tests/vectors/codec/NormalizationTest-15.0.0.txt and UNICODE-LICENSE.txt, and wrote the task record at tests/repair_22_33_1135.kvx; the task touches only src/codec/lxp_codec.c with planned path tests/codec, so the publication was held."
symptom = "do_4 asks for pinned Unicode NFC checking against the published vectors, which the touches list did not foresee; tests/vectors/codec holds five files on main and is the right home for the vectors and the license; the record belongs under tests/codec."
fix = "The touches list is amended to tests/codec and tests/vectors/codec and attempt 2 moves the record to tests/codec/repair_22_33_1135.kvx."

[gotcha.3295]
title = "Audit of the carried native source-control specification (spec/layerx-merge/source-control): 7 of the 34 original tasks are done (0.2, 0.3 to 0.7, 3.1), 26 are partial and 0.14 is not done; no original receipt exists in the snapshot because every build directory is ignored, the drivers under tests/<project>/cases/source_control bind git rev-parse HEAD of the host repository (the monorepo commit and root tree, not the project subtree), and the live-provider, model and object-store parts (0.11 to 0.14, 1.1, 6.1) exit BLOCKED or LIVE_EVIDENCE_REQUIRED without credentials."
symptom = "The specification was written for a standalone checkout; vendored, its receipts, revisions and ancestry checks point at history that is not in this repository."
fix = "Tasks 22.37.1 to 22.37.27 complete the unfinished originals under the moved directory after 22.36.1, with component-mode gates and the live parts recorded UNRUN (decision 2700); audit.kvx records every verdict."

[gotcha.3296]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 15: the independent executor run answers Fund Ok at 896330 CPU fuel while the kernel candidate Fund still refuses at pre-runtime with LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL (-3), recorded CPU fuel 0 and the terminal wrapper LXP/programs/pre-runtime-failure/v1 behind a context-hash prefix; the agent found that the native balance sight requires the receipt of the immediately preceding sequence and the current state root while the fixture still passed the CREATE receipt after block 1002 was finalized, bound a fresh receipt obtained through the idempotent rewards-account registration after finalization, added a kernel gas counter reading and synchronized a C node layout declared in both modules/lxphost/ctx.go and simulate.go; the build passed at cc579828686b96262c97dc0fe3c6b9d72ff41486 but the repair budget was exhausted before a verify run."
symptom = "The pre-runtime refusal is a stale receipt binding, not an executor or replay refusal (the executor path of decision 2647 passes); the correction has not run under a gate."
fix = "Attempt 16 requalifies the attempt-15 tree as it stands; the touches list gains programs/Cargo.lock for the dependency the fixture example added."

[gotcha.3297]
title = "22.33.1510 attempt 10: the fixture runs the real daemon library behind the recorded authority and the release reference resolves through TRACK (22.31.571), but both approval cases receive Corrupt from track_released at the first field of the answer. The daemon writes a TRACK observation as the 32-byte activity id, then the tracked submission of write_submission (services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs line 21778: the 32-byte submission id, the state code of state_code at line 18370, a 32-byte receipt digest for codes 6 and 9 or a 4-byte result code for code 7, the rung rank, the evidence count with text kind and 32-byte digest items, a zero transition count), then a zero receipt-presence byte. The Human decoder decode_tracked (services/human/crates/layerx-human-service/src/server/agent_runtime.rs line 4406) reads the submission reference as length-prefixed text, the code-6 receipt reference as text, and knows no code 9."
symptom = "The routing module of the daemon reads the same answer with 32-byte identifiers (lines 811 to 852) and the SDK contract names a 32-byte tx hash; the Human decoder was written against a text layout no producer serves, while the request side (hex text decoded by digest_from_hex) agrees on both sides, so only the answer layout diverges; the Human test agent_runtime_rungs.rs (lines 135 to 147) hand-encodes the same text layout and so never caught it."
fix = "Task 22.31.579 makes the Human decoder and that test follow the layout the daemon writes (decision 2701); 22.33.1510 requalifies after it."

[gotcha.3298]
title = "22.35.8 attempt 5: tsc passes and six of the seven vitest cases pass; pagesRenderInBothColourModes mounts Home, Transaction and Address in light and in dark mode under jsdom and took 66 seconds against the 60-second case timeout the spec sets (vi.setConfig at line 43), so the case failed as timed out and the production build was not reached."
symptom = "Six page mounts with the full provider tree, the mocked API and the token resolution cost about eleven seconds each in the qualification environment and one case carries all six."
fix = "Attempt 6 splits the case into one case per page with a 180-second timeout; the assertions stay."

[gotcha.3299]
title = "22.37.23 attempt 1 and 22.37.24 attempt 1: the build command (a pnpm filter on the control-services package) answered No projects matched the filters and exited zero without compiling anything; the vendored project directory excludes core/control-plane and core/kvx from its pnpm package set (pnpm-workspace.yaml) and builds that package standalone with npm --prefix core/control-plane ci --ignore-scripts and npm --prefix core/control-plane run build (Makefile lines 105 to 111), whose build script first copies the generated contracts module under src before tsc runs; without it dist/storage/runtime.js was missing, the standalone authority guard of 6_1.py failed before the component drill, and the recovery actor compile of 6_2.py stopped on the missing contracts module. The PostgreSQL 18 fixture server the drills need was present in the qualification environment."
symptom = "The series commands were derived from the package names, and the control-plane package is the one member of the vendored tree outside the pnpm package set."
fix = "Decision 2702 corrects the commands of 22.37.11, 22.37.12, 22.37.13, 22.37.22, 22.37.23 and 22.37.24 to the standalone npm build; 22.37.23 and 22.37.24 continue on their trees."

[gotcha.3300]
title = "22.33.1569 attempt 20: the MCP draw is refused as WalletToolError::Policy before any receipt; the policy engine answers Deny InvalidContext because valid_context (layerx-agentd policy/eval.rs lines 831 to 878) requires the authenticated cumulative use to belong to the session agent, and the scenario authenticates the cumulative use of the treasury DID of the fixture with the payer wallet account (tests/support/funded_scenario.rs lines 1005 to 1030) while the session agent and the executing wallet are the recipient (line 1043); the issue step authenticates the treasury correctly for its own session."
symptom = "authenticate_account_cumulative_use (protocol_evidence.rs) counts the entries of the named actor and binds the actor into the AuthenticatedCumulativeUse; valid_context compares that actor with session.agent and refuses on mismatch; the MCP draw session is the recipient, so the usage must be authenticated for the recipient DID and the recipient wallet account."
fix = "The draw steps authenticate the cumulative use of the session agent; the policy engine, the MCP tool and the daemon are unchanged."

[gotcha.3301]
title = "22.31.560 attempt 10: the fixture proof fails at native rate staging with canonical_digest_matches_envelope=false and preparation_id_matches_envelope=false while the actor matches, and the pending-use advance answers Ok(0); the log also shows observed_core_ms=1789365544000 against constraint_time=1789365544."
symptom = "Two production consumer defects. StagedNativeRateUse::stage (approval/native_program.rs line 1332) compares the envelope digest (Sha256 of the prepared canonical bytes) with binding.canonical_digest() and binding.preparation_id(), which hold the call identifier under decision 2634; the binding carries the envelope digest in its envelope_digest field (capability/binding.rs lines 2276 to 2278 and 2415 to 2417) and the sibling checks at lines 2430, 2476 and 2647 already compare against it. The prepare snapshot stores the block timestamp in seconds into protocol_timestamp (prepare/mod.rs line 569 from head.timestamp, documented as seconds in layerx-client sequencer.rs) while every consumer reads it as milliseconds (CoreTimestampMs, expires_at_ms comparisons at lines 6159, 6434 and 9231, the Human preview and session_control)."
fix = "The staging compares the envelope digest with the envelope digest of the binding, and the producer stores the core timestamp in milliseconds (decision 2704)."

[gotcha.3302]
title = "22.31.478 attempt 16: the after-guest Fund completes its CPU work (fuel 896330 under the 1000000 cap) and is refused at ledger apply with LXP_ERR_PROGRAM_REFUSED (-736) carrying callback stage 5 code -207, LXP_ERR_UNAUTHORIZED_DEBIT; the independent executor probe answers Ok because the executor applies no ledger leg."
symptom = "lxp_apply.c lines 103 to 116 admit a transfer leg only when exactly one transfer source authority of the call names authorized_from equal to the leg source account; the programs module builds those authorities from the declared transfer set of the call (src/modules/programs/call.c lines 2322 to 2412: one authority per declared leg with the kind of its declared source), and the Go fixture (rpc/repair_478_test.go) declares capabilities 3, 7 and 8 only, no transfer capability and no transfer leg for the Fund deposit, so the deposit leg finds no authority."
fix = "The fixture declares the transfer capability and the transfer leg of the Fund deposit as the production path does; a host-module omission in that path is a repair within the task touches."

[gotcha.3303]
title = "22.37.1 attempt 1: the layout driver test passes (6 cases) and the carried driver 0_8.py answers status BLOCKED with 3 assertions, 2 missing evidence kinds (the nonpublishing release startup and the prepared image) and no regression, exiting 2 (line 439 of the driver); the missing kinds are the live parts the series leaves UNRUN under decision 2700, so the verify failed on an outcome the series expects."
symptom = "The carried drivers distinguish BLOCKED (exit 2, missing live evidence) from FAIL (exit 1, a regression); the verify command treated both as failure."
fix = "A verify that runs a carried driver accepts exit 2 and refuses exit 1 (decision 2703); the task record names the missing evidence kinds."

[gotcha.3304]
title = "22.37.16, 22.37.19, 22.37.20 and 22.37.22 attempt 1: every pnpm typecheck or vitest run of the series stopped on modules the vendored tree generates or links at install time: the generated profile module of the process utilities library, the generated theme and export manifest of the plugin build package, the generated templates package, the domain package and the control-plane dependencies (Cannot find module pg, implicit any across src/agents and src/artifacts); 22.37.22 also lost the generated contracts module the control-plane build script copies under src because the build never ran before the native actor compile."
symptom = "The qualification environment installs the repository root node packages only; the vendored tree has two package managers (the control-plane package outside the pnpm package set with its own lock, gotcha 3299, and a pnpm workspace of 111 projects whose install runs the root prepare generation for the templates, plugin build and server packages in about 100 seconds) and the process utilities generate script sits outside that prepare filter."
fix = "Every series build command prepares the vendored tree explicitly (decision 2705): pnpm install with the frozen lockfile, the process utilities generate script, then the control-plane npm ci and build."

[gotcha.3305]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 1: the chunk-root boundary leaves build and the ten market tests pass, then the carried suite program_replay fails actual_module_start_refuses_unobservable_start_state (tests/program_replay.rs line 208): a module-start snapshot with capture enabled now answers Ok where the engine must map the observer refusal to UnreachableExecuted; the agent repaired it by refusing module-start snapshots before the profiled entry invocation, the repair compiled, and the gate ledger had no verify run left, so the 128-call proof never ran."
symptom = "The streamed capture replaced capture_program_record_from_store and started observing before the pre-start refusal the engine relies on; the final tree carries the repair unverified."
fix = "Requalify the final tree as it stands; the module-start assertion stays."

[gotcha.3306]
title = "22.31.217 attempt 8: 12 cases pass and 6 fail. Three Snapshot refusals (lines 1461, 1564 and 1629) come from read_native_effect_budget_sources (budget/program_sources.rs line 564) refusing caps.level() below STATE_PROVEN while CommittedCaps::level answers the retired CHECKPOINT_FINALISED (read/committed.rs lines 166 and 420), which the lattice orders below every current level (verify.rs compare): decision 2694 already assigns that repair to 22.31.560, so the three cases wait on it. Two MalformedPayload refusals (line 769) route the deploy and exitValue constructs through prepare_bound, which the binder table (layerx-crypto disclosure/call.rs lines 102 to 127) does not contain, as the attempt-7 ruling already said. One MalformedPayload refusal (line 549) is the create-source construct encoded by the production ABI encoder and refused by the production binder; the refusing word is not yet named."
symptom = "The level refusal is the producer defect of decision 2694, not a fixture matter; the two lifecycle constructs must never meet the binder; the create-source refusal needs the binder word index before any repair."
fix = "Continue after 22.31.560 with the three case classes separated; the create-source probe names the word or records a producer-to-consumer defect."

[gotcha.3307]
title = "22.37.21 attempt 1: the first control-plane build stopped on TS7034 and TS7005 (the validated legacy-map array at import.ts lines 1012 and 1042 without an element type) and the repaired build passed; the verify driver 5_2.py then reached the contribution checks and the strict deep-equality assertion at line 598 of the native source import actor failed although every field matched: the candidate scope read back through the source HTTP transport is a null-prototype object while the actor compares it with a plain object literal. The agent changed both sides of that comparison to canonical bytes, rebuilt (exit 0) and had no verify run left."
symptom = "The canonical JSON decoder of the source contracts module builds every object with Object.create(null) (contracts.ts line 113), so anything that crosses the transport comes back without a prototype; assert.deepEqual under node:assert/strict is deepStrictEqual and compares prototypes before fields. The decoder behaviour is deliberate (no prototype pollution) and is not a defect."
fix = "Proofs over transport-decoded source objects compare canonical content (decision 2706); the attempt tree requalifies as it stands."

[gotcha.3308]
title = "22.37.9 attempt 1: the control-plane build passed twice; the first verify stopped on a missing expected rejection at line 199 of the objects storage fixture (a test-input mistake the agent corrected); the second verify passed the 1_1.py component run (COMPONENT_PASS, 18 assertion groups, the 4096-entry patch metrics) and then the 0_1.py driver of the source-control cases raised FileNotFoundError for /root/.nvm/versions/node/v24.22.0/bin/node, the default it uses when its node override variable is unset; the qualification environment provides node 24.22.0 on the path under a different prefix."
symptom = "Six drivers of the source-control cases carry that home-directory path of the original author as a literal or as the default of an environment override (0_1.py line 119, 1_3.py line 125, 2_2.py line 191, 0_4.py line 96, 0_14_live.py line 23, 0_14_setup.py line 17); 0_8.py line 180 already resolves node through the override or shutil.which. The series gates of 22.37.8, 22.37.9, 22.37.11, 22.37.13 and 22.37.7 run the drivers with the literal path and would all stop the same way."
fix = "Drivers resolve node from the override variable they already read, else shutil.which on the path, and fail with a named message when neither resolves (decision 2707); the owners of the drivers make the change and 22.37.9 requalifies after 22.37.8."

[gotcha.3309]
title = "22.37.23 attempt 2 and 22.37.24 attempt 2: with the corrected build commands both builds passed and both verifies passed (the 6_1.py component drill with PROCESS_LOSS and PRIMARY_INSTANCE_LOSS PASS, FAILURE_DOMAIN_LOSS UNRUN; the 6_2.py workload checks), then the graph check refused the task because every entry of its symbols list is a file name (6_1.py, native_source_recovery_actor.mjs, routing.ts; campaign.mjs, native_source_external_workload.mjs, native_source_workload.mjs, storage_observer.mjs) and no such symbol exists in the graph; the agents correctly declined to edit the task record."
symptom = "All 27 symbols lists of the series 22.37.1 to 22.37.27 were written as file names when the series was authored; the graph check (spec.c line 4000) resolves each entry as a code symbol, and 3593 landed tasks carry an empty symbols list, which the check accepts. The live attempts 22.37.1 a2, 22.37.19 a2, 22.37.20 a2 and 22.37.22 a2 carry the old lists in their trees and will be refused the same way after a passing verify."
fix = "Every series symbols list becomes empty (decision 2708); the two attempts requalify on their trees and the live ones requalify as they report."

[gotcha.3310]
title = "22.37.16 attempt 2: the corrected build command passed (pnpm install, the profile module, the control-plane build) and the verify stopped at line 13 of the native source graph actor of the support directory: readFile of the vendored root path named like the project raised ENOENT; the graph actor, the signed transport, the qualification lanes and the roster graph scope of the support directory all execute that root binary, which the vendored tree ignores (.gitignore line 45) and the default make target builds from core/native with the tree-sitter runtime (Makefile lines 13 to 35: BIN and the cg compatibility alias, linked against sqlite3, curl and crypto)."
symptom = "The vendored project ships its CLI as a built artefact, never as a checked-in file; the series build commands prepared the packages (decision 2705) but not the native CLI, so the drivers of 22.37.16 (3_3.py), 22.37.18 (4_2.py), 22.37.19 (4_3.py) and 22.37.26 (7_1.py, which packages the root binary through release.sh) cannot run."
fix = "Those four build commands build the default make target of the vendored tree before the package steps that need it (decision 2709); the qualification environment provides the C headers the link needs; 22.37.16 attempt 2 requalifies on its tree."

[gotcha.3311]
title = "22.37.19 attempt 2: the build command passed the control-plane build and the host-daemon typecheck, then the source-control plugin typecheck reported 26 errors in app.tsx: TS2307 on the app entry of the plugin SDK package at line 6 and TS7006 implicit any on every parameter typed through it; the task record calls the declarations pre-existing and missing; no verify ran."
symptom = "The plugin SDK package (sdk/plugins of the vendored tree) exports its types from a bundled-types directory that Git ignores (.gitignore line 96) and that its build:types script produces with rollup over the sources; the plugin resolves the SDK through the package exports to that bundle, and a direct pnpm filter typecheck runs tsrs without the turbo dependency on the SDK type bundle that turbo.json declares for other consumers (lines 26, 32 and 554)."
fix = "The build command builds the SDK type bundle before the plugin typecheck (decision 2710)."

[gotcha.3312]
title = "22.37.22 attempt 2: the build passed twice; the first verify stopped on an authorization request that omitted the path its capability covered (corrected); the second reached the quiesce case and the isolation observer answered LEGACY_VISIBILITY_UNAVAILABLE, Cannot inspect every visible process storage handle and mapping; the final driver adjustment (no extra user namespace when the driver runs as root) is unverified."
symptom = "The observer in core/control-plane/src/migration/legacy.ts enumerates every pid of /proc and, for a pid that still exists, maps every error other than ENOENT on its stat, namespace link, mountinfo, descriptors or maps to that refusal without naming the pid, the file or the error code (line 187), so the record cannot say what was uninspectable; the 5_3.py driver re-executes itself as pid 1 of a private pid namespace with a private /proc and reaps no orphan, so a grandchild that outlives its parent stays listed as defunct, and a defunct process has no namespace link or mountinfo (ENOENT and EINVAL on a pid that still exists)."
fix = "The refusal detail names the pid, the file and the error code; a defunct process (state Z or X in its stat) is skipped since it holds no descriptor or mapping; the driver reaps orphans as pid 1 (decision 2711)."

[gotcha.3313]
title = "22.31.577 attempt 2 (the attempt-1 tree under the corrected environment): build, dependent-crate check and the earlier suites passed; two cases of repair_22_31_577.rs failed at lines 157 and 352 with EngineFault program replay record refused: Bounds while executing the 128-call guest under a profile of 4096 boundaries and 1048576 bytes; the task record is empty on the point."
symptom = "ReplayWitnessError::Bounds is raised at nine capture sites (the leaf count and byte appends of from_captured in replay_record.rs, the remaining-bytes, fuel-sum and step-index checks after captured_leaf in execute.rs around lines 1154 to 1196, the leaf decode) and the fault reason built at execute.rs line 1086 prints only the variant, so the record cannot say which bound a 128-boundary capture of a 17-page memory crossed."
fix = "The fault reason names the refusing check with its numbers; a boundary leaf carries the chunk root and the chunks the step changed, never the pre memory the previous leaf rebuilds (decision 2712)."

[gotcha.3314]
title = "22.37.20 attempt 2: the build passed twice after a PostgreSQL regex constraint repair; the second verify failed at native_source_git_actor.mjs line 1057 where assert.deepEqual compares the publication the SDK client decoded (a null-prototype object) with the service object the resume returned; the plugin tests were not reached."
symptom = "Decision 2706 applies: the canonical JSON decoder of the transport yields null-prototype objects (contracts.ts line 113) and strict deep equality distinguishes them from service objects."
fix = "The proof compares canonical bytes; the actor is audited for every other strict deep equality between a client result and a service object."
